7.3 Can the agent automatically retrieve MRPL knowledge?

No, not through the normal core agent path.

The RAG service exposes HTTP endpoints, but ConversationRuntime does not automatically invoke /v1/query. The current industrial demo has a separate MCP search_knowledge tool, but it performs local keyword search over Markdown:

for path in DATA.rglob("*.md"):
    ...

at demo/mcp_server/server.py:127-134.

That is not the same as integrated semantic RAG over an MRPL corpus.

The current complete retrieval path is:

Agent
  -> mcp__industrial_demo__search_knowledge
  -> Python DATA/*.md scan
  -> substring/word matching
  -> first 5 text snippets

It is not:

Agent
  -> integrated retrieval policy
  -> document corpus
  -> OCR/layout extraction
  -> embeddings
  -> vector search
  -> reranking
  -> page/region citation
  -> grounded answer

