23. What Not to Build

Stop or deprioritize

1. Unrelated educational HTML pages

   They do not improve SIH26117 evaluation probability.
2. More decorative presentation templates

   The current PPTX generation is enough to prove the concept. Additional visual polish is lower value than safe document ingestion and provenance.
3. Generic web/search features

   They directly conflict with the sovereignty story unless disabled and explicitly separated from sovereign mode.
4. More provider aliases

   The problem is not the number of provider names. The problem is deterministic local task routing and verified local inference.
5. More generic agent orchestration features

   The runtime already has substantial planning/subagent/task capability. Further generic orchestration will score less than an industrial workflow.

Features that look impressive but are low value

- More agent personas without stronger policy controls.
- More UI polish without real evidence citations.
- More synthetic decks.
- More abstract plugin lifecycle features.
- More model aliases.
- More generic chat memory.
- More remote-service integration.
- More protocol support without security isolation.
- A dashboard that displays claims rather than verified runtime facts.

